## Medals Counter – C++

📁 [`Medals_counter_Cpp/`](Medals_counter_Cpp)

Processes a stream of medal records (`event`, `medal 1–3`, `year`) and answers queries such as *"how many gold medals?"* or *"how many medals in chess in 2023?"* – with any subset of the three criteria.

**Highlights**
- Each record is indexed under **all 2³ = 8 combinations of criteria** in an `unordered_map` with a custom tuple hash (boost-style `hash_combine`), so every query is answered in **O(1)**.
- Strict line validation with `std::regex` (multi-word event names, year ranges without leading zeros); malformed lines are reported as `ERROR <line>` without stopping processing.

**Run**
```bash
g++ -std=c++20 -O2 Medals_counter_Cpp/medals.cpp -o medals
printf "Chess 1 2024\nChess 2 2023\n? Chess\n" | ./medals
```

